  "power_note": "N=5 gives a minimum resolvable difference of 1.00-9.70pp against a 0.50pp tolerance, so only the symmetric baseline resolves (23.18 sigma). Arms B/C/D sit at 0.38/1.75/0.46 sigma - none can be declared a miss. What IS established: removing skew costs 24.69pp (symmetric 29.44% vs real 4.74%), and restoring it closes ~93% of that gap (skewed_gamma 6.59%). Whether a skewed i.i.d. family suffices to +/-0.5pp needs roughly N>=50 for empirical_shuffle and N>=1900 for skewed_gamma at its observed dispersion.",
